Subject: Online/Ghost account: a 15-character name or 8-digit PIN survives a restart

Online round 2 (D-105). The Online Lobbies (and Ghost Trials) account is kept in
pd.ini as Mod.GhostUser / Mod.GhostPin (and the remembered accounts' numbered
keys). They were registered with max_str = GHOSTNET_MAXUSER (15) and
GHOSTNET_MAXPIN (8), and config.c's CFG_STR load copies max_str - 1 characters:
an account made with the longest name the page allows ("3-15 characters") or
the longest PIN came back one character short at the next launch, and the
automatic sign-in answered "Wrong username or PIN." every time. Found on the
lane-3 simulator: a 15-character test account name was read back 14 long.

The buffers are MAX + 2 (ghostnet.c), so registering MAX + 1 keeps every
character. Not iOS-guarded: desktop has the same bug; one for upstream.

--- a/port/src/main.c
+++ b/port/src/main.c
@@ -608,13 +608,17 @@
 	configRegisterInt("Mod.CharacterMissionDefault", &g_ModCiMissionDefault, 0, 1);
 	configRegisterInt("Mod.CharacterFilter", &g_ModCiCharFilter, 0, MODGHOST_CHRSET_ALL);
 
+	// (overlay 0063: config.c's CFG_STR loads max_str - 1 characters, so a
+	// maximum of GHOSTNET_MAXUSER/MAXPIN read back one short - a 15-character
+	// account name or an 8-digit PIN failed "Wrong username or PIN" on every
+	// launch after the first. The buffers are MAX + 2, so MAX + 1 fits.)
 	// The leaderboard account. The PIN is stored as typed, which is what a PIN
 	// with no password behind it amounts to - it is a claim on a name on a
 	// game leaderboard, not a credential worth protecting on disk. It travels
 	// over TLS and the server rate limits guesses, which is where the actual
 	// protection is.
-	configRegisterString("Mod.GhostUser", g_GhostNetUser, GHOSTNET_MAXUSER);
-	configRegisterString("Mod.GhostPin", g_GhostNetPin, GHOSTNET_MAXPIN);
+	configRegisterString("Mod.GhostUser", g_GhostNetUser, GHOSTNET_MAXUSER + 1);
+	configRegisterString("Mod.GhostPin", g_GhostNetPin, GHOSTNET_MAXPIN + 1);
 
 	// The accounts this machine remembers besides the active one. Numbered
 	// from two so that Mod.GhostUser stays the one in use and a pd.ini written
@@ -623,10 +627,10 @@
 		char key[32];
 
 		snprintf(key, sizeof(key), "Mod.GhostUser%d", i + 2);
-		configRegisterString(key, g_GhostNetSavedUser[i], GHOSTNET_MAXUSER);
+		configRegisterString(key, g_GhostNetSavedUser[i], GHOSTNET_MAXUSER + 1);
 
 		snprintf(key, sizeof(key), "Mod.GhostPin%d", i + 2);
-		configRegisterString(key, g_GhostNetSavedPin[i], GHOSTNET_MAXPIN);
+		configRegisterString(key, g_GhostNetSavedPin[i], GHOSTNET_MAXPIN + 1);
 
 		// Each remembered account keeps its own character, in the same range
 		// as the active one above. Without these, switching accounts brought
